  "output": "Now I have everything I need. Here's the full performance analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis — HR Policy Bot\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Pattern: `GET /api/queries/{query_id}`\n\n**File**: `src/api/routes.py:140-147`\n\nFour sequential DB calls, each opening and closing its own SQLite connection:\n\n```python\nquery = await db.get_query(query_id)              # connection 1\nagent_responses = await db.get_agent_responses(query_id)    # connection 2\norchestrator_response = await db.get_orchestrator_response(query_id)  # connection 3\nfeedback = await db.get_feedback_for_query(query_id)        # connection 4\n```\n\n**Fix** — parallelize with `asyncio.gather()`:\n\n```python\nquery, agent_responses, orchestrator_response, feedback = await asyncio.gather(\n    db.get_query(query_id),\n    db.get_agent_responses(query_id),\n    db.get_orchestrator_response(query_id),\n    db.get_feedback_for_query(query_id),\n)\nif query is None:\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Query not found\")\n```\n\n**Same pattern** in health check (`routes.py:93-98`): two SQL queries run sequentially inside one connection — already fine since they share a connection, no change needed there.\n\n---\n\n### 2. No React — but redundant DOM queries on every keystroke\n\n**File**: `static/js/app.js:62-66` + `469-472`\n\n`isProcessing()` does a live DOM querySelector on every key press:\n\n```javascript\n// Called on every 'input' event:\nsendButton.disabled = !hasText || isProcessing();\n\nfunction isProcessing() {\n    return !!currentQueryId &&\n           agentList.querySelector('.status-dot[data-status=\"working\"]') !== null;\n}\n```\n\n**Fix** — track state in a variable, update it only when state actually changes:\n\n```javascript\nlet processingState = false;\n\nfunction setProcessing(val) {\n    processingState = val;\n    sendButton.disabled = queryInput.value.trim().length === 0 || val;\n    sendButton.style.opacity = (!val && queryInput.value.trim()) ? '1' : '0.6';\n}\n\nfunction isProcessing() { return processingState; }\n```\n\nCall `setProcessing(true)` in `submitQuery()` and `setProcessing(false)` in `resetProcessingState()`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Response chunk rendering causes per-chunk DOM reflow\n\n**File**: `static/js/app.js:172-183`\n\nEvery streamed chunk fires an immediate DOM update:\n\n```javascript\ntextEl.textContent += data.chunk;\nscrollToBottom();\n```\n\nFor a 2,000-token response in 50-char chunks, that's ~100 sequential layout/paint cycles.\n\n**Fix** — buffer chunks and flush on `requestAnimationFrame`:\n\n```javascript\nlet chunkBuffer = '';\nlet rafPending = false;\n\nfunction handleResponseChunk(data) {\n    let messageEl = chatHistory.querySelector('.message.system:last-of-type');\n    if (!messageEl) {\n        messageEl = createMessage('system', '', currentQueryId);\n        chatHistory.appendChild(messageEl);\n    }\n    chunkBuffer += data.chunk;\n    if (!rafPending) {\n        rafPending = true;\n        requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n            messageEl.querySelector('.message-text').textContent += chunkBuffer;\n            chunkBuffer = '';\n            rafPending = false;\n            scrollToBottom();\n        });\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Duplicate agent name map — wasted memory and maintenance risk\n\n**File**: `static/js/app.js:22-32` vs `332-342`\n\n`AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES` (line 22) is declared at module scope, then a second identical `agentNames` object is created inline inside `renderCitations()` on every call:\n\n```javascript\n// Line 22 — module scope\nconst AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES = { orchestrator: 'Orchestrator', staffing: '...', ... };\n\n// Line 332 — recreated every renderCitations() call\nconst agentNames = { staffing: 'Staffing & Recruitment', ... };\n```\n\n**Fix** — remove `agentNames` and use `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES` directly in `renderCitations()`:\n\n```javascript\n// line 348 becomes:\n${AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES[agentId] || agentId}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Caching opportunity: policy registry loaded from disk 8 times\n\n**File**: `src/agents/specialist.py:72-75`\n\nEach `SpecialistAgent.__init__` reads and JSON-parses the registry file:\n\n```python\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n        registry = json.load(f)  # 8 separate disk reads + parse\n    return [r for r in registry if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\nSince `get_specialists()` is a singleton, this only happens once at warmup — but it still does 8 file reads where 1 would do.\n\n**Fix** — cache the registry at module level:\n\n```python\n_REGISTRY_CACHE: list[dict] | None = None\n\ndef _get_registry() -> list[dict]:\n    global _REGISTRY_CACHE\n    if _REGISTRY_CACHE is None:\n        with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n            _REGISTRY_CACHE = json.load(f)\n    return _REGISTRY_CACHE\n\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    return [r for r in _get_registry() if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Cache cleanup never runs — unbounded growth\n\n**File**: `src/data/db.py:358-368` + `src/main.py`\n\n`clear_expired()` exists and works correctly but is never called anywhere. The `fetch_cache` table grows indefinitely.\n\n**Fix** — call it at startup and add a periodic cleanup. In `src/main.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def _periodic_cache_cleanup(db: DatabaseManager, interval_hours: int = 24) -> None:\n    while True:\n        await asyncio.sleep(interval_hours * 3600)\n        deleted = await db.clear_expired()\n        logger.info(\"Cache cleanup: removed %d expired entries\", deleted)\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    db = DatabaseManager()\n    await db.initialize()\n    deleted = await db.clear_expired()  # clean on startup\n    logger.info(\"Startup cache cleanup: %d entries removed\", deleted)\n    task = asyncio.create_task(_periodic_cache_cleanup(db))\n    yield\n    task.cancel()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Memory leak risk: WebSocket reconnect loop can duplicate\n\n**File**: `static/js/app.js:90-98`\n\nIf `ws.onclose` fires while a previous `setTimeout(connectWebSocket, 3000)` is still pending (e.g., rapid connect/disconnect), multiple reconnect loops run simultaneously:\n\n```javascript\nws.onclose = () => {\n    setTimeout(connectWebSocket, 3000);  // no guard\n};\n```\n\n**Fix** — clear any pending reconnect timer before scheduling a new one:\n\n```javascript\nlet reconnectTimer = null;\n\nws.onclose = () => {\n    if (reconnectTimer) clearTimeout(reconnectTimer);\n    reconnectTimer = setTimeout(() => {\n        reconnectTimer = null;\n        connectWebSocket();\n    }, 3000);\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. Redundant JSON extraction pattern — copy-pasted three times\n\n**Files**: `src/agents/specialist.py:145-151`, `src/agents/orchestrator.py:148-154`, `src/agents/orchestrator.py:309-315`\n\nThe same `find('{')` / `rfind('}')` extraction is duplicated in three places:\n\n```python\ntext = raw.strip()\nstart = text.find('{')\nif start > 0:\n    text = text[start:]\nend = text.rfind('}')\nif end >= 0:\n    text = text[:end + 1]\nparsed = json.loads(text)\n```\n\n**Fix** — extract to `src/llm/client.py` or a `src/utils.py`:\n\n```python\ndef extract_json(text: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Extract and parse the first complete JSON object from an LLM response.\"\"\"\n    text = text.strip()\n    start = text.find('{')\n    if start > 0:\n        text = text[start:]\n    end = text.rfind('}')\n    if end >= 0:\n        text = text[:end + 1]\n    return json.loads(text)\n```\n\nThis is also a correctness fix — if the LLM wraps output in a markdown fence, the current code handles it; a shared utility ensures all callers benefit from any future improvements.\n\n---\n\n### 9. DatabaseManager instantiated fresh on every request\n\n**File**: `src/api/routes.py:125, 138, 167, 180`\n\n```python\ndb = DatabaseManager()  # repeated in every handler\n```\n\n`DatabaseManager.__init__` calls `_db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` — a syscall on every request.\n\n**Fix** — make it a module-level singleton initialized at startup:\n\n```python\n# src/data/db.py — add at bottom\n_db_manager: DatabaseManager | None = None\n\ndef get_db() -> DatabaseManager:\n    global _db_manager\n    if _db_manager is None:\n        _db_manager = DatabaseManager()\n    return _db_manager\n```\n\nThen in routes: `db = get_db()` instead of `db = DatabaseManager()`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| # | File | Lines | Severity | Category | Fix |\n|---|------|-------|----------|----------|-----|\n| 1 | `routes.py` | 140-147 | **High** | N+1 queries | `asyncio.gather()` all 4 DB calls |\n| 2 | `app.js` | 62-66, 469-472 | Medium | Redundant DOM queries | Track `processingState` as boolean |\n| 3 | `app.js` | 172-183 | Medium | DOM reflow per chunk | Buffer chunks with `requestAnimationFrame` |\n| 4 | `app.js` | 332-342 | Low | Redundant allocation | Reuse `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES` |\n| 5 | `specialist.py` | 72-75 | Low | Repeated disk I/O | Module-level registry cache |\n| 6 | `db.py` / `main.py` | 358-368 | **High** | Unbounded cache growth | Schedule `clear_expired()` at startup |\n| 7 | `app.js` | 90-98 | Medium | Potential memory leak | Guard reconnect timer with clearTimeout |\n| 8 | `specialist.py`, `orchestrator.py` | multiple | Low | Redundant code | Extract `extract_json()` utility |\n| 9 | `routes.py` | 125,138,167,180 | Low | Unnecessary syscalls | `DatabaseManager` singleton |\n\nIssues 1 and 6 are the highest-impact changes — the sequential DB calls add round-trip latency to every query history fetch, and the growing cache will eventually degrade SQLite lookup performance.\n",
